@startuml acp-turn
!include theme.iuml
title Crafty — separate ACP sessions and a FreeCAD evidence loop
autonumber

actor User
participant "Browser" as UI
participant "API / durable coordinator" as API
participant "Conversational Codex\nsession A container + local MCP" as Convo
participant "CAD Codex\nsession B container + local MCP" as Cad
participant "FreeCAD service\nbounded attempts" as FC

note over API, Cad
  Runtime orchestration restores each session's own volumes.
  Each supervisor negotiates ACP and configures its local MCP.
  Session creation and recovery: sessions diagram.
end note

User -> UI : capture / annotate images; describe repair
UI -> API : upload assets; submit message(clientMessageId, assetIds)
API -> API : persist message + work request + dispatch record
API -> Convo : session/prompt(text + asset references)
Convo -> API : asset_fetch(assetId)
API --> Convo : bytes -> local workspace path
Convo -> Convo : open local image; establish intent / measurements

opt more input needed
  Convo -> API : request_input(images, labels, fields)
  API --> UI : durable form / capture request
  note over UI, Convo
    Tool returns promptly. User submission becomes a later turn.
    No tool call waits indefinitely for a person.
  end note
end

Convo -> API : delegate_cad(objective, inputs, criteria, parentRevision)
API -> API : persist task + target CAD session + work request link
API --> Convo : taskId (prompt may finish while task continues)
API -> Cad : ensure session B; session/prompt(task context)

loop CAD agent's bounded iteration
  Cad -> API : fetch relevant assets into session B workspace
  API --> Cad : own local file copies
  Cad -> Cad : write / revise FreeCAD Python
  Cad -> API : cad_evaluate(sourcePath, params, outputs, checks, views)
  API -> API : freeze inputs; create run + attempt
  API -> FC : leased evaluation with frozen inputs
  FC -> FC : build geometry; render views; compute numerical evidence
  opt requested preview / export
    FC -> FC : derive GLB / STEP from evaluated geometry; check export
  end
  FC -> API : completed files + per-output status + check report
  API -> API : verify current attempt / generation / cancellation
  Cad -> API : cad_status / bounded cad_wait; fetch completed files
  API --> Cad : local image / report paths; optional GLB / STEP
  Cad -> Cad : open renders; read numerical checks; decide next iteration
  Cad -> API : result_publish(localPaths, sourceRevisionId, runId)
  API -> API : freeze bytes; commit immutable result + event once
  API --> UI : result.available(images / measurements / optional model)
end

Cad -> API : task_result(evidenceIds, interpretation, clarification?)
API -> API : persist handoff; deliver once at session A turn boundary
API -> Convo : next permitted prompt with CAD task result
Convo -> API : fetch returned images when visual inspection is needed
API --> Convo : files in session A workspace
Convo -> API : streamed response / task summary
API --> UI : explanation + referenced result cards

opt user stops active work (at any stage)
  UI -> API : stop(workRequestId)
  API -> API : cancel task tree; revoke further publication
  API -> Convo : session/cancel if its prompt is active
  API -> Cad : session/cancel if its prompt is active
  API -> FC : stop associated attempts
  note over API, FC
    Resolve pending protocol permissions as cancelled.
    Original prompt responses finish active ACP turns.
    Prevent queued handoffs from restarting cancelled work.
    Preserve published results and each session's mounted state.
  end note
end

UI -> API : reconnect(after event cursor)
API --> UI : replay durable application events
@enduml
